{
  "prompt": "We are building a SaaS tool for remote teams and have existing blog content about productivity hacks, but our current popups show up too early and get complaints. First, analyze our ideal customer profile and the specific problems our product solves to identify a high-value lead magnet that matches their awareness stage. Then, design a popup strategy that times this offer to appear only when users are genuinely engaged, ensuring it feels helpful rather than intrusive."
}

{
  "prompt": "We have an existing analytics setup and a product marketing document outlining our key business decisions. First, review that context to identify which specific events we need to track for those decisions, then implement the tracking with consistent naming conventions and validate the results by computing totals through two independent methods rather than just eyeballing the data."
}

{
"prompt": "I have a cloud workspace with an existing user authentication module and I want to add social login providers before we start building anything, please interview me one question at a time to clarify my target users, specific success criteria, and binding constraints so we can avoid assumptions. Once we agree on the requirements, write an implementation plan for a new engineer who hasn't seen our codebase, mapping out the file structure and breaking it into bite-sized tasks that follow test-first development principles."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to build a React component where an image slides in when it enters the viewport, and the animation reverses when it leaves, but I want to avoid using selectors that might break on re-renders by ensuring the animation is scoped correctly to the specific DOM node."
}

{
  "prompt": "Design a self-hosted funnel for our new product using Autonnel on Cloudflare Workers to avoid server management costs, and simultaneously set up the required server-side conversion tracking flow with click IDs persisted from the landing page through to the final order report in Meta Events Manager."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before deploying my new funnel to Cloudflare Workers using the Autonnel framework, please outline a plan that first captures click IDs and UTM parameters on the initial landing page hit and persists them server-side for every step. After defining this data flow, create a test case in JSON format that simulates the server-to-server purchase event report with deduplicated event IDs to verify our conversion tracking matches our internal order records."
}

{
"prompt": \"I need to extract pricing tables and changelogs from a known documentation URL, but I also need to interact with their search form to filter results by region before scraping the final page. Please use the `markdown` format for the extracted content and ensure you set `maxAge: 0` to guarantee we get the freshest version of the page.\"
}

{
  "prompt": "Please run a full site download of https://docs.example.com in markdown and screenshot formats, limiting it to the /features and /sdks sections while excluding all translation paths, then immediately follow up by crawling that same domain with a depth limit of three to extract any additional linked pages into a JSON output file."
}

{
  "prompt": "First, extract the pricing table from our known documentation page at docs.example.com using markdown format to get the base data. Then, if the extracted content reveals a paywall or requires clicking into specific subscription tiers to see full details, use browser interaction to navigate those hidden sections and collect the complete pricing information."
}

{
"prompt": "I have a draft email for our new feature launch, but I'm not sure if the hypothesis behind it is strong enough to justify an A/B test. First, help me refine the underlying assumption and predicted outcome into a clear hypothesis that isolates one variable. Then, take the full draft and run a systematic set of focused editing passes to improve clarity, flow, and persuasiveness without changing the core message."
}

{
  "prompt": "I have an existing agent project that I deployed imperatively, and now I need to enable comprehensive observability with prompt-response logging and BigQuery analytics. Please guide me through the process of first verifying if my current deployment conflicts with Terraform-managed infrastructure, determining whether I need to delete and restart or simply update environment variables and IAM roles, and then executing the necessary steps to provision the required resources before finalizing the deployment."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please set up an anti-detect browser profile using the antibrow SDK to ensure consistent device fingerprints, then use the agent-browser CLI to load the core skill and launch a Chromium instance that automatically retrieves the latest workflow instructions."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to set up a new React 19 website in my local workspace that uses Higgsfield authentication but does not include any AI content generation features, ensuring the final product displays only my own brand and avoids using Higgsfield-specific design tokens or badges."
}

{
  "prompt": "Using the antibrow MCP server via npm, have the AI agent navigate to my test site to verify that two separate profiles maintain distinct timezones and WebRTC configurations without leaking any shared identity data across them."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to create a character design sheet showing front, side, and back views of a woman with short red hair and a blue jacket, ensuring the character looks identical in every view. Please start by planning the workflow to ensure consistency, then generate the initial reference image using an appropriate AI model, and finally produce the remaining angles while maintaining that same identity throughout."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please plan a landing page for my SaaS product by first searching the web to find current trends and competitor examples, then using those insights to generate a hero image that matches the style of top-performing pages."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to design a statistically valid A/B test for our new checkout flow that predicts a 10% increase in completion rates based on user feedback about missing steps, while also generating fresh ad headlines and descriptions for social media platforms to drive traffic to the landing page where this test will run."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to generate a talking-head video of a character speaking from an audio file, and then extend that clip to make it longer while keeping the motion and lighting consistent."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to find the latest news on AI agent development, extract key details from the top search results into a markdown file, and then use that extracted information as input to generate a realistic image of a futuristic office scene using a text-to-image model."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before processing my video, run `npx hyperframes skills update embedded-captions` to ensure the latest version is active, then generate captions using the Standard theme which places most text on a lower-third rail and only embeds key climax words directly behind the subject."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before we design an A/B test for our new checkout button, please review the product marketing context to understand our current funnel constraints, then help me draft a statistically rigorous hypothesis that isolates a single variable while defining primary and guardrail metrics. After finalizing the test structure, create a corresponding Meta Ads campaign strategy that targets our ideal customer segment with a specific CPA goal, ensuring we avoid angles or audiences already listed in the marketing learnings section."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to build a solution that handles long-running document processing workflows and stores the results in an object storage bucket. Please first recommend the specific Cloudflare products best suited for this job and explain why they fit my needs, then generate the complete code using the Cloudflare CLI (cf) to set up these services."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before merging the pull request for the new file upload feature in our Next.js application, please perform a multi-axis review to ensure correctness and readability, then apply threat modeling principles to identify spoofing and tampering risks in how external inputs are handled."
}

{
  "prompt": "We're seeing a 5% monthly voluntary churn rate and need to set up an automated system in HubSpot that scans our usage data weekly to identify at-risk customers, then automatically triggers personalized save offers via email before they cancel. Please start by outlining the specific product marketing context we should review first, and then define the full workflow including the trigger conditions, step-by-step actions, and a self-check mechanism to ensure we're only contacting users who meet our activation threshold."
}

{
"prompt": "I'm building a GSAP animation where I need to sequence several tweens using a timeline with specific position offsets, and I also want to use utility functions to clamp mouse coordinates between 0 and 100 before applying them as values in the tween."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to set up a new project using the HyperFrames CLI on my local machine, then find an existing animation blueprint for a brand reveal before composing a custom GSAP timeline with two specific atomic rules to achieve a staggered headline effect."
}

{
"prompt": "Based on the findings from our latest Notion marketing audit, please outline a comprehensive 12-month growth strategy using the AARRR framework that aligns with our current budget and team capacity, then separately design a scalable programmatic SEO approach for our template library that prioritizes proprietary data and clean URL structures to avoid thin content penalties."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to set up a new HyperFrames project and quickly find a pre-made blueprint for a brand reveal animation, then modify it by adding a specific GSAP rule that reveals text one line at a time. Please use the CLI to initialize the project with an example, search the catalog for the closest matching primitive effect, load the relevant blueprint from the index, and finally compose the final timeline using atomic rules while ensuring I run linting checks after each structural change."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before generating the video, generate a vector ledger in JSON format that maps every seam transition, text entry cascade, and cursor-led action to specific curve parameters, then stamp this master ledger into the final HTML file using the provided seam-stamp script."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to build a new AI-powered customer support agent on Azure using Microsoft Foundry; please start by writing the required deployment plan file in markdown format as your first step, then run the dependency check script and read the specific workflow guide before executing any commands."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please review the existing video edit script in JSON format to identify any logic issues, then use the RunComfy CLI tool on our platform to extend the canvas of the resulting video from 9:16 to 16:9 while preserving the central action and generating a new output file."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before drafting a new campaign strategy for our SaaS product, please consult the product marketing context file and then convene a council session with three conflicting marketing advisors to debate the approach and identify key trade-offs. After synthesizing their disagreement into a clear decision path, apply a seven-sweep copy editing pass to refine the resulting proposal, ensuring brand voice consistency while improving clarity."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before installing the grain-overlay component or setting up a new composition, first review the plugin execution rules in the HyperFrames documentation, then use the CLI to add the block and wire it into my HTML file with the correct data attributes."
}

{
"prompt": "I'm building a React component where I need to animate draggable elements with FLIP transformations and scroll-linked reveals using GSAP; please write the code showing how to register the required plugins first, then create tweens that combine core timeline sequencing with the Flip and ScrollTrigger effects."
}

{
"prompt": "Execute the provided plan for refactoring the authentication module in our Git repository, proving each step by writing a failing test before implementing the fix, and narrate your progress briefly between tool calls without pausing to check in with me; once you finish all tasks, announce that you are using the finishing-a-development-branch skill to complete this work, run the full test suite to verify everything passes, detect if we are in a normal repo or a named branch worktree, and present the appropriate merge options for finalizing the branch."
}

{
"prompt": "Before generating the animation, verify the `general-video` skill is up to date using `npx hyperframes skills update general-video`, then check if my Figma link needs `/figma` processing. If I have a brand-reveal need, load the matching blueprint from `blueprints-index.md`; otherwise, compose 2-4 atomic rules into a paused GSAP timeline without guessing usage limits."
}

{
  "prompt": "First, run a natural language search for recent federal regulations on AI data privacy to find relevant government sources, then use the scrape ID from one of those results to interactively log into the specific agency's compliance portal and extract their latest enforcement guidelines."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before we start, run the update check for the general-video skill and confirm it's current, then verify my HyperFrames auth status. If I'm signed out and no offline provider exists, stop; otherwise, compare my Figma link against the blueprints-index.md to decide if I should load a multi-phase blueprint or compose atomic rules from the rules-index.md."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before I start setting up my HyperFrames plugin, please walk me through the required installation steps to ensure everything is ready. Once that's done, help me build a motion sequence by combining two atomic animation rules with a paused GSAP timeline, and then switch to using an existing blueprint from the index when the scene needs a complex multi-phase choreography instead of building it from scratch."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please set up a CI check using GitHub Actions that runs a headless fingerprint scan on Node 22, saves the JSON output as an artifact, and compares it against a baseline to catch any regressions in our Chromium-based test browser. Additionally, write a unit test that integrates with our existing Playwright page objects to verify that the harness's JavaScript environment matches its network-layer view without modifying the browser or adding evasion profiles."
}

{
"prompt": "Before we start, please run `npx hyperframes skills update motion-graphics` to confirm the latest version is installed. Then, using a Figma design URL provided below, export the assets and translate any Motion animations into GSAP code, generating a short, design-led motion graphic under 10 seconds."
}

{
"prompt": "Before generating the motion graphic, run `npx hyperframes skills update motion-graphics` to ensure the latest mechanics are available, then if the logo comes from a Figma URL, use `/figma` to export assets and brand tokens before building the short, design-led piece."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please explore potential code changes for inserting a new adapter module into our isolated PyTorch training script and document the candidate modifications, then execute the selected short-run verification command using the existing Docker environment to generate the training logs and status summary."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before creating a new organization via the Clerk API, please verify that the CLERK_SECRET_KEY is set and check if my current BAPI scopes include write permissions, warning me if I need to rerun with --admin. Then, set up a webhook handler in Next.js for user creation events that uses verifyWebhook() from @clerk/nextjs/webhooks, ensuring the route stays public without auth protection."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please plan a test-first development workflow to generate a short intro video from text, then extend it into a longer scene while maintaining visual consistency. Once the full clip is ready in MP4 format, debug any runtime errors by reviewing the CLI logs and provide the exact runcomfy commands used for both steps."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to build a new feature for our React application that includes both user authentication and a real-time dashboard. Before writing any code, please create a structured specification document in Markdown that defines the acceptance criteria for each independent capability and maps out the required tasks. After we review and approve this spec, use an incremental approach where you implement one vertical slice—like the login flow first—and test it immediately before moving to the next part."
}

{
"prompt": "Run a full browser fingerprint audit on my local Chrome instance to identify discrepancies between the client and network views, then interpret the results by grouping failures into their specific sources like launch configuration or page-modifying layers while ignoring expected issues from headless mode."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to set up a new Cloudflare project for an agent that handles routing, but I'm unsure whether to use Wrangler or the cf CLI. Once you help me pick the right tool and configure it based on my goal, please also run a performance audit using Chrome DevTools MCP to check Core Web Vitals, making sure to verify available tools first before analyzing the site."
}

{
  "prompt": "I'm launching a $97 digital course via paid Instagram ads and need to build a complete sales funnel from scratch; please first create a ready-to-implement blueprint specifying every page, message, price point, and success metric before we discuss how to optimize the live landing page once it's running."
}

{
"prompt": "Before we start, please install the belt CLI and then execute a Python script that loads the 'requests' library to verify it's available. Once confirmed, use the RunComfy video generation tool with an AI model to create a 5-second clip of a futuristic city from a text description, and finally apply the intelligent video editing feature to swap the background while keeping the original subject consistent."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before generating a new video with subtitles in .srt format using Remotion, please check the project manifest to preserve my recent manual edits and then upgrade all Remotion dependencies to their latest compatible versions by inspecting the lockfile."
}

{
"prompt": "I'm integrating Firecrawl into my Node.js app for the first time, so please run the CLI initialization command with all features and browser auth to set up my API key in the environment file. Once that's ready, I need you to extract content from https://firecrawl.dev using markdown format while ignoring navigation elements, but ensure the data is fresh by forcing a new read rather than using cached results."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please use the firecrawl CLI to first map out the documentation section at https://docs.example.com with screenshots, then run a targeted crawl on just the /features and /sdks paths, and finally scrape the main content from any resulting pages that require JavaScript rendering."
}

{
"prompt": "Please use the `agent-browser` CLI to fetch the specialized skill for deriving an API client from a HAR file, then leverage the `browser-act-skill-forge` to automatically generate a verified Python script that extracts product pricing data from our own Shopify store by observing what's visible on the page, and finally configure the `antibrow` anti-detect browser SDK with a frozen real-device fingerprint in JSON format to run this new agent on a Linux server without triggering bot detection."
}

{
"prompt": "First, use the anti-detect browser SDK to spin up a fresh profile with a real-device fingerprint, then run a verification checklist on that profile to catch mechanical failures like mismatched timezones or WebRTC leaks before we start testing. Once the profile passes all isolation checks and is confirmed internally consistent, load the agent-browser CLI to execute an exploratory QA workflow that captures accessibility snapshots and compact element references for our automated testing session."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to extract pricing tables from our competitor's public website at scale; please first use the browser-act-skill-forge tool to explore the site and generate a verified Python script that only reads visible data, then execute it using agent-browser with an anti-detect browser instance created via the antibrow package to ensure consistent fingerprints across runs."
}

{
  "prompt": "I have a concept for a hold-to-delete button that I need explored in several genuinely different directions so I can see which approach works best."
}

{
"prompt": "I need you to generate a new presentation deck with a specific widescreen layout, apply a red background without using hash symbols for the color code, and ensure the content fits entirely within the slide boundaries."
}

{
  "prompt": "Set up push notifications for my user's mailbox so that new emails are streamed as JSON lines in real time."
}

{
"prompt": "Set up a multi-agent workflow where one coordinator breaks down a complex task into subtasks, assigns them to workers, waits for completion, and then aggregates the results before reporting back to me."
}

{
"prompt": "I have a square portrait photo that needs to be transformed into a wider landscape image, extending the background seamlessly while keeping the subject unchanged."
}

{
"prompt": "I have a Vercel access token stored in my environment or .env file, along with the project ID and team information I need to deploy my application. Please find the token from either the environment variable or the configuration file, then use it to configure the CLI for deployment without ever passing the secret as an argument on the command line."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please check if my explainer video setup is up to date, then take a provided text about blockchain and build it into a faceless explainer video with no captured assets. Make sure you follow the strict step-by-step workflow starting from setting up the project configuration, planning the story, designing the visual style, creating the script and audio plan, generating frame-by-frame visuals using sub-agents, and finally assembling the output."
}

{
"prompt": "I need a content strategy for my new SaaS product that targets B2B decision-makers on LinkedIn, focusing on generating qualified leads while maintaining an authoritative yet approachable tone."
}

{
  "prompt": "I have a Cloudflare Worker and need to send transactional emails using the platform's email service without managing API keys. Please guide me through verifying that my domain is enabled, configuring the necessary bindings in wrangler.jsonc, and writing the code to send an email directly from the worker."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to generate an animated GIF for Slack that looks polished and creative, not basic. Please create an emoji-sized animation with dimensions of 128x128 pixels, keeping the frame rate between 10 and 30 fps and limiting the total duration to under three seconds. The design should use thicker lines for outlines to avoid a choppy look, incorporate visual depth through layered shapes or gradients, and feature interesting details like highlights or patterns rather than plain geometric forms."
}

{
"prompt": "I need help planning a new Kubernetes cluster for our production environment, including advice on networking setup, API server access controls, and initial security configurations."
}

{
"prompt": "Run a comprehensive audit across the entire codebase to identify any silent failures, duplicate logging, or violations of error wrapping and checking rules."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to build a new AI agent using the latest version of the Mastra framework. Please verify the current installation requirements and provide the exact steps to set up the project, ensuring you check for any recent API changes or deprecated patterns before writing any code."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to find where a specific function is defined and who calls it across my codebase, then surgically edit the implementation based on those findings before verifying the changes don't break anything."
}

{
"prompt": "I have a spreadsheet template where I need to calculate monthly revenue projections based on user-provided growth rates and initial figures. Please create a script that reads the input values, applies the specified formulas for compound annual growth calculations across the data rows, and outputs a final workbook with all results derived from those formulas rather than hardcoded numbers."
}

{
"prompt": "Prepare my Product Hunt listing by generating a hero image that shows the product in action with core value visible, researching competitor launches to inform our strategy, and creating a set of supporting images including a feature demo, a before-and-after comparison, social proof metrics, and a technical differentiator shot."
}

{
"prompt": "I'm building a Next.js app and want to ensure my data fetching strategy minimizes waterfall delays while optimizing bundle size for better load times. Can you review my code structure and suggest specific changes to parallelize independent requests, defer unused awaits, and conditionally load heavy components only when needed?"
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to design a new thumbnail for my latest video about sustainable gardening tips, featuring a bright outdoor scene with two people holding plants, and I want the final image to include a bold headline saying \"Grow Green\" in the top left corner."
}

{
  "prompt": "We need new sales collateral including a deck and objection-handling guide for our inside sales team targeting mid-market CTOs. Please start by asking me specific questions about our unique value proposition, current sales motion, existing materials, and what reps are currently struggling with before you write anything."
}

{
"prompt": "I have a set of UI animations that feel sluggish and generic; please review them using a specific format that compares the current implementation side-by-side with an improved version, explaining exactly why each change makes the interaction feel more natural."
}

{
  "prompt": "Please generate a video using the inference.sh CLI by running the google/veo-3-1-fast model with the prompt 'drone over mountains', and also upscale my local image at /path/to/photo.jpg by a factor of two using the falai/topaz-image-upscaler app."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to run a cost anomaly check for my AI agent usage and get the results in JSON format so I can review it programmatically."
}

{
"prompt": "Use the hyperframes media-use tool to find a copyright-free sound effect for a rain scene in my project folder, and tell me which file it found."
}

{
"prompt": "Generate a 15-second cinematic video using Kling 3.0's multi-shot feature with three distinct scenes, starting from an initial image and maintaining consistent character identity throughout."
}

{
  "prompt": "List any open issues or pull requests that have no category or state labels assigned yet."
}

{
"prompt": "Create a React 18 TypeScript dashboard with Tailwind CSS that includes a data table and charts, then bundle the entire application into a single self-contained HTML file so I can share it directly in this chat."
}

{
"prompt": "I have an existing AKS cluster and need to set up AI Runway from scratch, so please guide me through the full onboarding process step by step, starting with verifying my cluster's GPU compatibility before installing the controller."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to set up my Neon database connection for a new serverless web application using Drizzle ORM. Please list my available projects and help me pull the correct connection string with pooled access, then update my .env file with the DATABASE_URL variable without overwriting any other existing settings."
}

{
  "prompt": "Build a responsive Flutter dashboard that uses MediaQuery.sizeOf to detect window dimensions and LayoutBuilder to adjust the grid of charts based on maxWidth constraints instead of checking device orientation."
}

{
  "prompt": "We have an existing Azure subscription with current VNet and resource group setups that we need to extend; please inventory our live infrastructure, design a secure hub-spoke architecture for our new workload by wiring it into the existing network without modifying current resources, validate the generated Bicep code with local checks and security scans, show me the scan results, and get my approval before deploying only the new additive changes."
}

{
"prompt": "I need to automate posting to Twitter/X using the inference.sh CLI tool. Please help me generate an image with a specific prompt, extract the resulting URL, and then use that URL to create a new post on my Twitter account with custom text."
}

{
  "prompt": "I have a Cloudflare Workers project using the stable `@cloudflare/sandbox` package, but I need to run a long-running streaming process; please show me how to correctly use `startProcess` or `execStream` instead of blocking `sandbox.exec`, and ensure my container image matches the current stable release rather than the `next` preview."
}

{
  "prompt": "Before generating any code for my Cloudflare Workers app, please verify whether I am currently using the stable '@cloudflare/sandbox' package or if I've accidentally included the preview '@next' version in my dependencies."
}

{
  "prompt": "Generate a 5-second, 1080p video in a 16:9 aspect ratio of a person speaking based on the provided audio file at 'https://example.com/speech.mp3', ensuring their lip movements match the dialogue exactly."
}

{
  "prompt": "I need to run two specific analysis passes on my current project: first apply grilling to stress-test the logic, then follow up with domain modeling to refine the structure."
}

{
  "prompt": "Run a quick exploratory sweep on this dataset using the PyTorch toolkit to test small subsets with varied learning rates, then summarize the top candidates in a Markdown report that compares their results without certifying them as final solutions."
}

